course: dictionary
lesson: 2273
title: Cree: a people and a language
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one job. Cree can name a people, name a language, or describe something that belongs to those people. Look at the words around it to decide which one it is. «Native peoples of North America were many nations with hundreds of languages, such as the Cherokee, Navajo, Lakota, Haudenosaunee, Inuit and Cree.» Cree sits in a list of nations, so here it names a people.
explain: Context also helps with the describing job. «Cree syllabics» is a special kind of writing. The word Cree tells you which writing it is, so it is describing a thing, just as «English books» tells you which books.
explain: Notice the capital C. Cree is always written with a capital letter, because it is the name of a people and a language. Other names like English and French also start with capitals.
fact: Cree is the name of a First Nations (Indigenous) people of Canada.
fact: Some Cree people also live in the northern United States.
fact: Cree is also the name of the language, or group of related languages, that Cree people speak.
fact: «Cree syllabics» is a special writing system, used to write some Cree.
fact: Cree is written with a capital C because it is a name.
exercise: «The Cree are one of the largest First Nations groups in Canada.» What does Cree mean here? | A language only | A mountain range | A kind of weather | *A people
exercise: «She speaks Cree at home with her grandmother.» What is Cree in this sentence? | *A language | A kind of dance | A river | A town in Canada
exercise: Why does Cree start with a capital C? | *Because it is the name of a people and a language | Because it is a very long word | Because it is a sentence starter in every book | Because it is an important colour
test: «Cree syllabics were developed in the 1840s with Cree speakers.» Here Cree is describing the writing. What does it tell us? | A kind of food | *Which writing it is: Cree writing | A mountain | A town
test: Where do the Cree live? | Only in Quebec | *Across a large area of Canada, from the Rocky Mountains to Quebec, with some in the northern United States | Only in Europe | Only in the Rocky Mountains
exam: Which sentence uses Cree correctly? | The cree are a people of Canada. | The Cree is a bird that lives in Quebec. | Cree means a long, cold river. | *The Cree are a First Nations people of Canada.
